# 2장 (4판) 영어판: 퀘스트 ID -> (제목, 받을 때, 진행 중, 끝낼 때)
EN = {
"story_2_01": ("The Map of Twenty Years Ago",
 "I owe you the story of that map. Twenty years ago the Order sent an expedition to look in on the waking guardians. Twelve of us. I was captain; Kael was my second, my closest friend. …I'm the only one who came back. The eleven red marks are where the others fell. One has been erased. Kael's.",
 "Hear Captain Roran out.",
 "This time I go myself. Bad leg and all. Hell and the void were lands I didn't know. This is road I walked. Road I lost. Eleven name tags. If I bring back even one… no. I bring back all of them."),
"story_2_02": ("The First Page of the Logbook",
 "The first mark is a cave underground. Read the logbook's first page with me. Grottols live down there, timid things that carry ore on their backs and swallow anything that shines. The tags will be in their bellies. They bolt at the sound of a pick, so go quietly.",
 "Examine the first page of the logbook with Roran, then catch 2 grottols underground.",
 "Tomas, and Lia. In my own hand the log says only 'two, lost in the cave'. Wrong. Both tags came out of the same belly. They didn't get lost. One went back for the other. …For twenty years I've kept the wrong thing written down."),
"story_2_03": ("The Rusted Door",
 "At the end of the cave is the rusted knight's chamber. …I'll be honest. Twenty years ago I stood before that door and only watched the third one fall. Bren, our youngest. My leg locks up. I'm going anyway. Look hard at the doorway. Back then we were too busy fighting to see anything.",
 "Find the wrought chamber underground and examine what is left before the door.",
 "Bren's tag. Wedged between the stones. (Roran stands a long time holding it.) And those marks in the floor. So it hasn't taken one step in a thousand years. Facing forward. And we called it a 'monster'. Ask the smith. He's the one who reads armour."),
"story_2_04": ("The Back Left Open",
 "A piece of the rusted knight's armour? Let's see. …This isn't my family's work. Far older. Flame Knights' make. Odd, though. Bring me some iron. If I hammer the same shape I'll know.",
 "Bring 6 iron ingots to Bram the smith and hear how the armour was made.",
 "See? The front plate is three layers, the back one. That's no mistake. It was forged that way. Armour that trusted whoever would come up behind. Its lord was to return through the door at its back, so it left its back open. And striking that back is the only way. An ugly business."),
"story_2_05": ("The Sentinel of a Thousand Years",
 "The wrought knight. His name was Horus, they say. He waited a thousand years for one man. After the great swing of the axe his back is open. The back he left open. This time we have a Memory Gate. Put him to rest inside and the seal won't burst. If only we'd known twenty years ago. …Go. I'll stand at the door. This time I won't close my eyes.",
 "Open the Memory Gate and put the wrought knight to rest.",
 "As he fell he looked back for the first time, you say. At the door. Saw no one there and sank down. …I know that feeling. Twenty years I watched the north road from the dock. He was no monster. He just waited. Like me."),
"story_2_06": ("Spiral Abyss, Floor One",
 "I wrote Horus's name. But inside the helm a path was drawn. I followed it and it leads to the Order's old proving ground, the Spiral Abyss. Clear the first floor and you are a full member of the Order. They say the Abyss shows the memories of those who passed through. The Flame remembers. The expedition passed through too, before it left.",
 "Clear the first floor of the Spiral Abyss.",
 "What did you see? …The expedition's last night. The man called Kael holding a letter up to the fire. Then pressing the map into the captain's hands. A letter? What letter. …Don't tell the captain yet. Not until he brings it up himself."),
"story_2_07": ("The Lights of the Dark Wood",
 "The second mark is the dark wood. At night glowing things called lanterns drift there. The log says 'Marco, lured into the swamp by the lights.' My handwriting. Kill them and you get glowing jelly. Shine it on the tree trunks. Let's see whether I wrote this one right.",
 "Defeat 5 lanterns in the dark wood and bring 4 glowing jelly.",
 "Knife cuts on every tree, you say, in the jelly's light. Arrows. Marco wasn't lured. He marked his way as he walked. Hoping we'd follow. His tag was driven into the last trunk. …Wrong again. Twenty years I thought he died with his head in the clouds."),
"story_2_08": ("Kael's Scribbles",
 "Marco's arrows lead to the southern jungle. There's an old vine-covered temple there. Kael camped in it. He scribbled on every wall. I shouted at him for it. Defacing a ruin. …Let's read them. In the order he wrote them. Watch for foliaaths in the vines, man-eating flowers you don't see until you're close.",
 "Find a jungle temple, examine Kael's three scribbles in order, and defeat 3 foliaaths.",
 "The first was a joke. The second was arithmetic. The third… was to me. 'You go north.' He had already made up his mind in that temple to stay behind alone. What happened in between? What did you read, Kael."),
"story_2_09": ("The Dagger on the Cliff",
 "There are things that fly over the sea cliffs. Nagas, winged sea serpents. They spit poison. They got Ines. In the log I wrote 'Ines, charged recklessly'. Bring me their fangs. I'll make a dagger. Ines fought with a single dagger.",
 "Defeat 2 nagas on the sea cliffs and bring 2 naga fangs.",
 "(Roran grinds the fangs into a dagger.) A quiver lay beside the tag under the cliff, you say. Empty. …She didn't charge recklessly. She shot until the arrows ran out and then drew the dagger. Until those of us behind her got clear. I need to rewrite the log. All of it."),
"story_2_10": ("The Campfire",
 "Today we rest. We fill our bellies before the snowfields. Bring cooked mutton and sweet berries. The supper they liked best on the march. …I'll tell you about them while we eat. The things I never put in the log. Call the archivist too. She'll have things to write.",
 "Bring 4 cooked mutton and 6 sweet berries, and listen to Roran by the campfire.",
 "(Isabel wrote until the back of her hand was black.) …Strange. For twenty years I remembered them as a number. Eleven. Now I've said it they're people. Tomas couldn't whistle. That's written down somewhere now."),
"story_2_11": ("Heart of Ice",
 "I hear Roran is going to the northern snowfields himself. On that leg. …There's no stopping him. As it happens I have a request. A frost giant sleeps there holding a crystal of cold. To face fire we need a cold that can put fire to sleep. First find where the giant sleeps.",
 "Find where the frost giant sleeps in the snowfields.",
 "You found it. The giant sleeps deep. The crystal wakes when it feels fire. It will wake when you ember-bearers come near. …Tell Roran this. Don't look for Kael's sword in the snow. He won't find it. (The Elder did not say how he knew.)"),
"story_2_12": ("The Ones Left Standing",
 "Three marks in the snow. Danilo, Jonah, Fei. The log says 'blizzard, three missing'. We never found the bodies. But the hunters say that in a den deep in the snow the frozen dead stand in rows. As if someone stood them up. Let's go. They may be standing there.",
 "Find the hideout in the snowfields, examine the rows of frozen dead, and defeat 4 frozen skeletons.",
 "Three scarves. Corps scarves. Standing for twenty years. Not lying down. …A strange feeling. I should be angry. Someone stood them up, the ones I thought the snow had buried. So they wouldn't be covered. I need to see what did it."),
"story_2_13": ("The Undertaker of the Snow",
 "That's the one. The hunters call it Skor. An old word for 'the one who does not cover'. A yeti. When it finds something frozen dead it carries it to the den and stands it up. It believes that what the snow covers is forgotten. To it we are thieves, come to take what it stood up. It is no guardian bound to a seal. No gate needed. Still, a captain collects his own tags. Clear the way.",
 "In the snowfield hideout, put Skor the yeti to rest. (Deal at least 10% of its health.)",
 "Before it fell it stepped in front of those three, you say. To the last. …I took the three tags. I left the scarves. I left them standing. Beside the one that stood them up. Uncovered. (Roran strikes a line in the log and rewrites it. Over 'missing': 'gathered by Skor'.)"),
"story_2_14": ("The Captain in the Blizzard",
 "Surveyor, the captain hasn't come back! He's sitting in front of the hideout, on the very spot where he lost three twenty years ago. And a blizzard is coming. I can't tell whether his leg is frozen and he can't get up, or he won't. Please take him a campfire and hot food. Please.",
 "Take 1 campfire and 6 cooked beef to Captain Roran in the blizzard.",
 "(Roran barely thaws his hands at the fire.) …It was here twenty years ago too. I lost three because there was no one to light a fire. I had the ember in my fist and my hands were too frozen to strike it. This time there's a fire. Because you're here. …To the giant. This time I'm not the one who waits."),
"story_2_15": ("The Giant That Holds the Ice",
 "Put the giant to rest and bring the ice crystal. Fight beyond a Memory Gate and the snowfield will not come down. When it draws breath, frost follows. Step aside. One day that crystal will matter very much. When fire is about to overtake someone.",
 "Open the Memory Gate and put the giant that holds the ice to rest.",
 "The crystal trembles in your hand. It feels fire. Keep it safe. Never sell it. …No sword in the nest? I thought not. Kael never came to the snow. (Having said it the Elder fell silent a moment, like a man who has said too much.)"),
"story_2_16": ("Eight Stones",
 "The next mark is a monastery on a high peak. The Chronicle speaks of 'the mason who carved the seals in stone', who cut a marker for each of the seven seals. Tongbi the sculptor, heir to that craft, is still on the mountain. The patterns for those stones should be in the yard. Count them for me. There should be seven.",
 "Find the mountaintop monastery and examine the stones in its yard.",
 "Eight? …The Chronicle says seven. And only the eighth has no name. Not erased. Never carved. Like the empty shelf in the stronghold library. I must ask the mason himself. The captain… is at the foot of the mountain. He says he can't climb this one."),
"story_2_17": ("The Captain at the Foot of the Mountain",
 "…I'm not going up. It isn't the leg. Twenty years ago I lost two on that mountain. Hayun and Otto. They fell from the sculptor's pillars. I told them 'go up'. I only watched from below. If I stand there again I'll send someone up again.",
 "Talk to Captain Roran.",
 "(Isabel lays a hand on Roran's shoulder.) \"You aren't sending us up, Captain. We're climbing.\" …All right. Then this time I hold the rope at the bottom. Not just watch. If you fall, I catch you."),
"story_2_18": ("The Stone Without a Name",
 "Pass Tongbi the sculptor's trial. Climb the rising pillars and keep your balance. He looks for balance, not strength. When it's done, ask him about the eighth stone. The captain is holding the rope below.",
 "Pass Tongbi the sculptor's trial.",
 "\"The eighth stone was cut by my master's master's master. He heard the name to carve, he said, and forgot it between picking up the chisel and striking. So he wrote 'waiting'. To carve it the day he remembered.\" …Forgotten. Not erased. And two tags lay one on the other under the pillar. Tell the captain. Tell him we came down."),
"story_2_19": ("The Beast That Howls at the Moon",
 "Every night a beast howls on the southern plain. A different voice as the moon waxes and wanes. Kael picked up a cub on the march and raised it. They say it's grown and carries Kael's scarf in its jaws. Fight it in the open and the pack comes. Call it alone through a Memory Gate. …Not killing, the archivist says. Putting to rest.",
 "Open the Memory Gate and put the beast that howls at the moon to rest.",
 "(Roran grips an old scarf.) Kael's. It carried this for twenty years. Never left the place its master set it down. …This land is full of things that wait. The knight at the door, the undertaker in the snow, this beast. And me. The scarf smells of sun. South."),
"story_2_20": ("The Second Sun",
 "In the southern savanna is the grove of the sun tribe. Masked warriors. They serve a 'second sun'. On the last page of the log there's a line in Kael's hand: 'Under the sun the ember can't be seen.' I took it for nonsense. Look closely at the masks. I need to know why they wear them.",
 "Find the sun tribe's grove, examine the masks, and defeat 6 masked warriors and 1 hunter.",
 "A name in every mask. So they carve the faces of their dead and wear them. So they aren't forgotten. And the sun is the fire that lights those names. …They're archivists too. Writing on wood instead of paper. And one priest half lifted his mask and asked, you say: 'Did you come carrying an ember? Then he's watching too.' A scar on the left cheek. Kael. …Who is watching, Kael."),
"story_2_22": ("The Face Under the Mask",
 "I have something to say. On the last night twenty years ago Kael pushed this map into my hands and said 'the southern sun is calling us, you go back north'. Nonsense. I lost my temper and left. Never looked back. For twenty years I thought he'd gone mad and abandoned me. He must think I abandoned him. What do I say when we meet?",
 "Talk to Captain Roran.",
 "…All right. I'll do as you say. Now to the sun chief. It holds Kael. Or maybe Kael holds it."),
"story_2_23": ("The Blazing Sun",
 "The sun chief. Head of the tribe. It guards the second sun. That is the tribe's memory, the fire that lights the names in the masks. To them we're the ones come to put it out. Kael stands beside it. Burned by twenty years of sun, he can no longer tell the chief's will from his own. He strikes whoever carries an ember. He'll strike me. Open the Memory Gate. Keep to the shade.",
 "Open the Memory Gate and put the sun chief to rest.",
 "The mask broke. Kael… was under that sun for twenty years. His body couldn't hold. At the end he looked at me and grinned. 'Did you count three times.' And then: 'It wasn't the captain who froze the sea.' I don't know what it means. You take the mask. I can't carry it."),
"story_2_24": ("The Letter Held to the Fire",
 "Kael's clumsy mask. The one with eleven notches inside. Please look under the pillar where it hung. The temple scribble said 'I held the letter to the fire'. I don't think he burned that letter. He was a man who kept evidence. Go with the captain. He shouldn't read it alone.",
 "In the sun tribe's grove find the letter Kael hid and examine it together with Roran.",
 "I held the captain back. He had his cane up and was going straight to the Order. This is what Kael burned twenty years to prevent. Confront him now and all of it is wasted. I'll keep the letter. Between the pages of the Chronicle. Nobody searches an archivist's book. …The Elder taught me my letters. That is his hand. No doubt."),
"story_2_25": ("Twelve Names",
 "Bring the tags you gathered. Ten. There's none for Kael. He left his tag in the temple. With his ember. We have the mask instead. …For twenty years I thought: when I've gathered them all I'll burn the roster. Burn it and let them go. I've lit the fire.",
 "Hand the 10 expedition name tags to Captain Roran.",
 "(Isabel catches Roran's hand as he reaches for the fire.) \"Burn it and they're forgotten, Captain. Fire eats names. Give it to me. I'll write them.\" …Right. That's the kind of world this is. (Roran holds out the roster. And the logbook.) Write this too. Every silly line they wrote. And fix the lines I got wrong."),
"story_2_26": ("The Rusted Vow",
 "The names are written. One thing is left. Why was Kael's mark erased from the map? Report the end of the expedition to the Elder. Don't mention the letter. The archivist is right. Not yet. I can't look him in the face. My cane would move first. You go. And watch his hands.",
 "Report the end of the expedition to Elder Erwin.",
 "(Erwin takes the map and draws a finger over Kael's place.) \"It was I who erased it. It was the Order's custom to erase beforehand the place one would not return from.\" Meaning he erased it before the expedition ever left. A faint heat rose from the glove. The Elder changed the subject. \"There is worse news. The ice of the northern sea is creeping toward the town. Go and see Oscar the fisherman.\""),
"story_2_06a": ("The Owner of the Empty Line",
 "We can fill the empty line! There were more names inside Horus's helm. Three posts their lord ordered to 'wait'. At the door, the squire Horus. At the place of the oath, Vice-Captain Helvar. The name from Bram's ledger. The fourth captain whose name was scorched away in the fortress. Helvar is an old word for 'the one who keeps hell's threshold'. Deep in Hell, in a soul sand valley, is the arena he guards. Read the writing by its door and tell me why he stayed alone.",
 "Find the Underworld Arena in Hell, examine the petition by its door, and defeat 3 knights who keep the oath.",
 "\"You cannot make a weapon out of your comrades.\" He alone opposed the oath by which three captains give their heads and become the Black Star. Overruled, he still did not leave. He guarded the place where it was sworn, so no one could take the three heads. …And we already took them. Not knowing that, he is still guarding the door."),
"story_2_06b": ("Helvar, the Underworld Knight",
 "Hell isn't my road. I don't know what's what down there. But that one I do know. A man guarding a post with nothing left to guard. Helvar is no guardian bound to a seal; he stayed on his own feet. No Memory Gate needed. No seal to burst. No mercy either. His knights carry the arena key. The mark on his back is his weakness, they say. Same as Horus. Their lord's people all leave their backs open.",
 "In the Underworld Arena, put Helvar the Underworld Knight to rest. (Deal at least 10% of his health.)",
 "He drove his sword into the floor and stepped aside as he fell, you say. After looking at the three empty stands in the middle of the arena. …He knew. That the three heads were already gone. He stood there anyway until someone came and told him it was over. (Roran says nothing for a long while.) Go to the archivist. Tell her to fill the empty line."),
"story_2_09a": ("The Sunken Road",
 "Kael's third scribble pointed south. Between the jungle and the sun lands lies the desert. The log says 'the caravan road collapsed, three days' detour'. We went around. Kael was alone, so he would have cut straight across. We never asked why the road collapses. Let's see what is under it.",
 "Find the sandworm's nest in the desert and examine what is left on the tunnel wall.",
 "A canal. So it's a beast that dug waterways under the desert. And it keeps digging to the plan even after the kingdom was buried. That's why the ground falls in where it passes. The plan ends 'as far as the king's garden', you say. …That garden was buried a thousand years ago. Another one that waits."),
"story_2_09b": ("That Which Calls the Water",
 "Sirok. It means no harm. It is just doing its work. Until the one who gave the order comes back and says 'enough'. But every time it digs, the caravan road falls in and people are buried. It isn't bound to a seal either. We fight it in the nest. The ground under your feet trembles before it bursts from the sand. Step away then. It spits poison. Bring antidotes.",
 "In the sandworm's nest, put Sirok the sandworm to rest. (Deal at least 10% of its health.)",
 "Water sprang up where it fell, you say. One thread of it. Water in the channel it dug for a thousand years, for the first time. …It never reached the garden. But it did call the water. Have the archivist write it down. 'The work is done.' There's no king left to tell it so."),
"story_2_18a": ("A Name Written in Claws",
 "The third post carved in Horus's helm. Horus at the door, Helvar at the place of the oath, and a tower. Beside the tower there are no letters, only claw marks. The signature of someone who cannot write. It is the dragon that Arden, the knight-commander, rode. There is a tower beyond the mountains. Go and see what remains in it. The captain is going too. 'I have to see the ones who wait,' he said.",
 "Find the dragon's tower, examine the banners and the saddle, and defeat 3 tower guards.",
 "It kept the saddle clean for a thousand years, you say. Burning the soot off with its breath. So its master could mount the moment he returned. …If the burning knight of the dreams is Arden, he cannot come back. He is a man with the fire shut inside him. Does the dragon know? Is it waiting without knowing, or knowing?"),
"story_2_18b": ("Until It Turns to Ash",
 "Ashlord. A dragon guarding the tower where its master said 'wait' and left. To it we are thieves in its master's tower. It has nothing to do with the seals either. We fight it in the tower. Its throat swells before it breathes fire. Get behind a pillar. The guards keep rising. Don't drag it out. …Whether it's right to put it to rest, I don't know. But I don't know that it's right to leave it waiting for someone who will never come, either. I say that as a man who did it for twenty years.",
 "In the dragon's tower, put Ashlord the infernal dragon to rest. (Deal at least 10% of its health.)",
 "At the end it fell across the saddle, you say. Covered it with a wing. Held its breath so as not to burn it. …Enough. No head count today. Let's just sit a while. And if you dream tonight, tell the archivist what that knight says."),
"story_2_06h1": ("A Thousand-Year Tab",
 "That ledger line you saw. 'Sword of Vice-Captain Helvar, repair. Payment when his lord returns.' It kept me up all night, so I went through the storeroom. It's there. The sword he left. A thousand years at the bottom of my family's storeroom. In two pieces. Not broken. Snapped on purpose. You can tell by the edge. I want to join it again. It's steel forged in hellfire, an ordinary forge won't heat it. Bring gold and blaze rods.",
 "Bring 4 gold ingots and 2 blaze rods to Bram the smith.",
 "It took. But look at the join. Bent over a knee and snapped. There's my grandfather's grandfather's hand in the margin of the ledger. 'The vice-captain came out of the council, snapped his own sword and left it. Said he would not carry a blade that would serve the oath. Said to mend it. Said he would come for it the day he could carry it again.' …He never came. In a thousand years."),
"story_2_06h2": ("The Watch Roster of a Thousand Years",
 "I want a closer look inside the arena. At what he did for a thousand years. Knowing how your opponent lives before you fight him is a captain's job. Twenty years ago I didn't do it. Walls, floors, wherever a man has lived long, his habits are left behind. Find them.",
 "In the Underworld Arena examine the roster on the wall and the empty stands in the middle.",
 "So every day at the same hour he polished three stands. Empty stands. And the last line of the roster. 'Today too my lord did not come. I stand again tomorrow.' He wrote that three hundred and sixty thousand times. …I counted twenty years, some seven thousand days. I've nothing to say in front of him. Bring Bram's sword. It's time it went back."),
"story_2_06h3": ("The Tab, Paid",
 "You're back. The sword… yes, he took it, you say. Before he fell he took it from your hands and looked at it a long while. Then drove it into the floor. Sit. The ledger must be closed. Striking out a thousand-year-old line happens once in a smith's life, if that. I called the archivist girl too. I strike out; she writes in.",
 "Watch Bram the smith close the ledger.",
 "'Paid.' Done. Paid with what? The sword went back to its owner. To a smith that's payment. …One more thing. There's another line in the ledger with the same crest. 'Saddle of Knight-Commander Arden, repair.' That one is marked collected. A dragon saddle. Which means there was a dragon."),
"story_2_09s1": ("The Calendar on the Dry Well",
 "Before crossing the desert we stop at the desert village. We did on the expedition too. You ask the road of those who live by it. An old man there said something odd back then. 'The road doesn't collapse, it sinks in order.' I let it pass. He said something was carved by the well. Let's go and read it.",
 "Find a desert village and examine what is carved on the stone by its well.",
 "Every date and place of collapse written down, you say. Three hundred years of them. And the interval never changes. Once every seventeen days, one stretch at a time, west to east. That's not collapse. That's someone working. To a calendar. …And the villagers call it 'the guest who calls the water'? Unafraid? Because grass comes up a few days later where it sank. Damp rising from below."),
"story_2_09s2": ("The King's Promise",
 "Amrat, King of the Desert. The Chronicle has one line: 'he took the eye in the sand'. Nothing about why he left the canals to a beast and went. The pyramid you saw in chapter one. It wasn't a tomb, they say, but the king's water store. There should be pictures on the wall. See what the king promised the beast. And take water with you when you go to the nest. You'll understand why once you've seen the pictures.",
 "Examine the wall paintings of the desert pyramid and bring 3 water buckets.",
 "So the king promised the beast as he left to receive the eye of the seal. 'I'll wait in the garden. The day the water reaches it I'll open the gate.' And as the price of the eye his kingdom went under the sand. The beast digs on, believing the promise. …The last panel. When it hears water it stops work and comes up, because the king used to pour water and tell it 'well done'. That's the water we're taking. Whether that's right on the way to a fight, I don't know."),
"story_2_18d1": ("The One Who Fed It",
 "On the lower floor of the tower is the guards' room. The ones who stand watch even dead. Who feed the dragon and rehang the banners. See what they fed it. A beast remembers the hand that fed it. Even on the way to putting it to rest, let's know whose hand it is waiting for.",
 "On the lower floor of the dragon's tower examine the guards' log and the basket.",
 "Apples, while its master was there. In Hell, of all places. Carried down from the surface every day. By the knight-commander himself. After he left, the log says, the dragon wouldn't eat them. It leaves them to rot and looks at the southern sky. On nights the southern sky is red, it cries. …The red sky we saw in chapter one. It knows where its master is. By the smell of the fire. It can't go. Because he said 'wait'."),
"story_2_18d2": ("The Words 'I Can't Come Back'",
 "I hear you put the dragon of the tower to rest. …Sit. Tell me the story from the start. The banners, the saddle, the basket by the window. I have never been to that tower. I know it only from books. So I want to hear it as you saw it.",
 "Tell Elder Erwin what you saw in the dragon's tower.",
 "(The Elder listened to the end and said nothing for a long while.) …The one who made them wait is the worst of it. Not the ones who waited. 'I'll be right back' is easy to say. Nobody says 'I can't come back'. As if saying it made it true. (He presses a gloved hand to his eyes.) You said it for him. To that dragon. Thank you. I mean it."),
"story_2_12k1": ("The Corpse Thief",
 "The snowfield hunters winter in igloos. They leave things on the walls. What they saw and where. Twenty years ago there was already talk of a 'corpse thief'. Bury a comrade lost to the blizzard and next day he's gone. I put it down to wolves. Let's read it again. To the end, this time.",
 "Find an igloo in the snowfields and examine what the hunters wrote on its wall.",
 "The graves weren't dug up. The snow was brushed aside, you say. By hand. A large hand. And the last entry. It carried a living man back and left him. Not a corpse thief, then. Something that tells the frozen dead from the freezing. It takes the dead and brings back the living. …Now I'm curious what it is."),
"story_2_12k2": ("The Standing Forest",
 "Standing the frozen dead upright. I found it in the Chronicle. It's the funeral of the Frost Kingdom. The ground there was frozen too hard for graves. So they froze their dead standing. In rows at the edge of the village. They called it 'the standing forest'. And there was a beast that helped. Look at the innermost wall of the den. What that beast was taught should still be there.",
 "Examine the innermost wall of the hideout in the snowfields.",
 "The Frost Kingdom froze whole when its king made himself a guardian. The undertakers too. Only the beast was left. Its teachers are gone and it still does as it was taught. Finds the frozen dead, stands them up, keeps them uncovered. Whoever they belong to. For a thousand years it has held the funerals of the whole snowfield alone. …I write names. Skor stands people up. It's the same work. Keeping them from being forgotten."),
"story_2_24a": ("The Folded Corner",
 "While I was slipping the letter into the Chronicle I noticed it. The bottom corner is folded over once more. Glued down. Kael didn't glue it. It was like that when the Elder sent it. I got it open. There is one more line. I've brought the captain. Please hear it with us. I don't trust myself to look at his face alone.",
 "Read the last line of the letter with Isabel the archivist and Captain Roran.",
 "The captain opened his notebook to the first page. 'The lode. Roof collapsed. Thomas, Lia.' He looked at that line for a long while and said, 'The roof never collapsed. I wrote it that way. Because I didn't know what it was.' …The Elder knew. What was down there. Something that is not a seal. He knew, and he still marked that cave as the first stop."),
"story_2_24b": ("The Discarded Plinth",
 "Before we go I want to check one thing. The Sculptor's monastery. The eighth plinth was empty, but the plinth itself is still there. A stone carver first cuts an under-inscription into the plinth. What will be carved on the stone that stands there. Lay paper on it and rub with charcoal and it shows. A rubbing. I'll give you the paper. Oh. No. Please bring the paper yourself. I used all mine on the Chronicle.",
 "At the Sculptor's monastery, lay paper on the eighth plinth and take a rubbing. (3 paper)",
 "You have it? Show me. …It isn't a name. The seven other plinths all have a king's name underneath, but the eighth has one word. In the old tongue. 'Chesed.' It means mercy. And the Sculptor wrote beside it, small: 'The name to carve is gone. I carve only what was received.' And below that, scratched in another hand: 'Throw it away. Deep.' With seven seals stamped round it. Oh, and this rolled out from under the plinth, you said. An eye cut from stone. The Sculptor left it there. Throw it into the air and it flies one way only. An eye that knows where its stone was thrown."),
"story_2_24c": ("Back to the First Cave",
 "We go. Under the first cave. The way I said 'down' twenty years ago. I walk in front again. Not to fight. To look. At what I failed to see that day. There will be marks. Lightning leaves marks on stone. We follow them in order. See one and the next will show.",
 "Find the cave under the lode and follow the marks of twenty years ago in order, with Roran.",
 "(Roran sits with his back to the cave wall, two helmets in his lap.) …Fused together. They stood back to back. Shielding each other. I didn't see that either. I was blind by then. That hum from further in, you hear it. It hummed twenty years ago too. I took it for the ringing in my own ears."),
"story_2_24d": ("The Axe and the Mirror Stone",
 "Roran told me. A stone that throws lightning underground. Felix drew the inner cave. Crystal pillars rising, the thing in the middle, polished slabs set in the walls. To a smith's eye that is no battlefield. It's a furnace. A furnace that holds lightning. And a furnace can be worked. Bring me two iron axes. I'll regrind the edges to the angle that breaks crystal. No charge.",
 "Bring 2 iron axes to Bram the smith, and hear how to work the inner cave.",
 "The edges are set. Don't forget. The order is everything. Break the crystal, carry the lightning, stand before the mirror stone. And one more thing. I told Roran, and you hear it too. That is no guardian. Nobody raised it. It was thrown away and it grew. So no one will thank you for putting it to rest, and no one will blame you. That is the loneliest kind of fight."),
"story_2_24e": ("Head Count",
 "I've lit a fire at the cave mouth. The same spot as twenty years ago. Twelve of us sat round it then. Kael put too much salt in the soup and Bren ate all of it. Sit a while before we go down. That time we just went down. Didn't even count. Bring bread and roast meat. This time we eat first.",
 "Bring 4 bread and 4 cooked mutton and talk with Roran by the fire at the cave mouth.",
 "If you've eaten, up. Head count. Two. …No. (Roran opens his notebook. He lays the ten tags round the fire one by one. In the empty place he sets the clumsy mask.) Twelve. This time we all go down together. What they didn't see twenty years ago, they see today with us. Move."),
"story_2_24f": ("The Stone That Was Given No Name",
 "At the very back of the cave is the place that wakes it. Go close and you will see what is written about it. Read, then go in. Remember what Bram said. Crystals with the axe, carry the lightning, stand before the mirror stone. The four standing stones first. I hold the entrance. With this leg I'm a burden inside. But this time I stand at the door to the end. I'll see who falls behind.",
 "Put Chesed to rest in the cave under the lode. (Start the fight at the summoning place at the very back. Everyone who fights there is credited.)",
 "It split. The dark blue stuff fell away like ash. Only white stone was left. A well-cut stone the height of a man. One word carved on it, and beneath that an empty space for a name. Room for eight letters. The archivist measured. …For a thousand years something else filled that space. The forgotten. We set Thomas's and Lia's helmets down in front of the stone. It seemed the right place. Up we go. There's a roster to finish."),
}
